course: dictionary
lesson: 4325
title: Grown: a form of grow, or an adult
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word grown has two jobs. After has, have or had, it is a form of grow, as in «She has grown taller since the summer.» Plants and animals also grow, so «Rice is grown in China» tells you that rice is produced by growing.
explain: As an adjective, grown means adult, as in «a grown man» or «grown-ups». Context helps you choose. Swap in your meaning: «Grown-ups sometimes cannot keep promises» still makes sense with adults, so grown-ups means adults.
explain: Always check the words around grown. If it follows has, have or had, or sits after is, it is probably a form of grow. If it stands before a noun like man or ups, it probably means adult.
fact: Grown is the past participle of grow: grow, grew, grown.
fact: «Has grown» and «had grown» show that something changed over time.
fact: «A grown man» and «grown-ups» mean adults.
fact: «Fully grown» means completely developed, with nothing more to grow.
fact: «Home-grown» means grown at home or nearby, as in home-grown tomatoes.
exercise: What does grown mean in «She has grown taller»? | Adult | Planted in soil | Green and leafy | *The form of grow used after has
exercise: «A grown man lifted the heavy bag.» What does grown mean here? | *Adult | Has become taller | Planted in soil | Happy
exercise: Find and copy the word that means adults in «Grown-ups sometimes cannot keep promises, because things change.» | promises | things | change | *Grown-ups
test: What does «home-grown» tomatoes mean? | Bought from a shop far away | *Grown at home or nearby | Red and round | Very tall
test: In «a child sitting far out can lift a grown-up sitting close in», what does grown-up mean? | A small toy | Something that cannot move | A tree | *An adult
exam: Which sentence uses grown to mean adult? | Rice is grown in China | *Dad is a grown man | She has grown taller | Plants have grown from seeds
